### Deviation from the literal claim "root set matches base X.hxml"

The f32 root sets are **not** byte-equal to the base sets: each base hxml additionally roots
`registry.Main` (kotlin.hxml:239, rust.hxml:233, swift.hxml:232), which the f32 files omit.
This is **documented as a deliberate exception** in `f32-roots-fix/REPORT.md` (§1.1: registry.Main
is the binary64 packaging/demo entry, no test cases, f32 gen trees carry no Main artifact) and is
covered by 3 exemptions in `tools/roots-guard/roots-allowlist.json`. Note therefore that the
"guard-postfix-PASS" is **PASS with 3 exemptions in force** (`roots guard: PASS (3 exemption(s)
in force)`), not an unconditional equality PASS. This does not affect test-id comparison
(registry.Main contributes no test ids), but the claim "root set matches its base counterpart"
is true only modulo this documented, exempted exception.

